{"name":"Moonraker","hex":"#c0b2d7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Moonraker","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of moonraker (“someone from Wiltshire”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Moonraker"}],"entries":[{"title":"Moonrakers","blocks":[{"text":"Moonrakers is the colloquial name for people from Wiltshire, a county in the West Country of England. It derives from a story of smugglers pretending to be catching the moon's reflection in a pond, using a rake."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Wiltshire_Moorakers_postcard_detail.jpg/330px-Wiltshire_Moorakers_postcard_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moonrakers","wikidata":"Q3323601"},{"title":"Moonraker (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Moonraker is the third novel by the British author Ian Fleming to feature his fictional British Secret Service agent James Bond. It was published by Jonathan Cape on 5 April 1955 and featured a cover design conceived by Fleming. The plot is derived from a Fleming screenplay that was too short for a full novel, so he added the passage of the bridge game between Bond and the industrialist Hugo Drax. In the latter half of the novel, Bond is seconded to Drax's staff as the businessman builds the Moonraker, a prototype missile designed to defend England. Unknown to Bond, Drax is German, an ex-Nazi now working for the Soviets; his plan is to build the rocket, arm it with a nuclear warhead, and fire it at London. Uniquely for a Bond novel, Moonraker is set entirely in Britain, which raised comments from some readers, complaining about the lack of exotic locations."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/ba/MoonRakerFirst.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moonraker_(novel)","wikidata":"Q603310"},{"title":"Moonraker (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Moonraker is a 1979 spy-fi film, the eleventh in the James Bond series produced by Eon Productions, and the fourth to star Roger Moore as the fictional MI6 agent James Bond. The third and final film in the series to be directed by Lewis Gilbert, it co-stars Lois Chiles, Michael Lonsdale, Corinne Cléry and Richard Kiel. In the film, Bond investigates the vanishing of a Space Shuttle orbiter, leading him to Hugo Drax, the owner of the shuttle's manufacturing firm. Along with astronaut Dr. Holly Goodhead, Bond follows the mystery from California to Venice, Rio de Janeiro, the Amazon rainforest, and finally into outer space to prevent a plot to wipe out the world population and repopulate humanity with a master race."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/66/Moonraker_%28UK_cinema_poster%29.jpg/330px-Moonraker_%28UK_cinema_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moonraker_(film)","wikidata":"Q334780"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/The_Crammer%2C_Devizes%2C_England.jpg/500px-The_Crammer%2C_Devizes%2C_England.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/The_Crammer%2C_Devizes%2C_England.jpg/500px-The_Crammer%2C_Devizes%2C_England.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Crammer, Devizes","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Crammer%2C_Devizes%2C_England.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Sign_for_the_Moonrakers%2C_Stratton%2C_Swindon_-_geograph.org.uk_-_6266638.jpg/500px-Sign_for_the_Moonrakers%2C_Stratton%2C_Swindon_-_geograph.org.uk_-_6266638.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Sign_for_the_Moonrakers%2C_Stratton%2C_Swindon_-_geograph.org.uk_-_6266638.jpg/500px-Sign_for_the_Moonrakers%2C_Stratton%2C_Swindon_-_geograph.org.uk_-_6266638.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASign_for_the_Moonrakers%2C_Stratton%2C_Swindon_-_geograph.org.uk_-_6266638.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Moonrakers_sign_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5522114.jpg/500px-Moonrakers_sign_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5522114.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Moonrakers_sign_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5522114.jpg/1280px-Moonrakers_sign_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5522114.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Moonrakers_sign_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5522114.jpg/500px-Moonrakers_sign_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5522114.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMoonrakers_sign_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5522114.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Bundesarchiv_Bild_141-1880%2C_Peenem%C3%BCnde%2C_Start_einer_V2.jpg/500px-Bundesarchiv_Bild_141-1880%2C_Peenem%C3%BCnde%2C_Start_einer_V2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Bundesarchiv_Bild_141-1880%2C_Peenem%C3%BCnde%2C_Start_einer_V2.jpg/500px-Bundesarchiv_Bild_141-1880%2C_Peenem%C3%BCnde%2C_Start_einer_V2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A V-2 rocket launch from summer 1943: the threat remembered from the war was the basis of the novel.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABundesarchiv_Bild_141-1880%2C_Peenem%C3%BCnde%2C_Start_einer_V2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedi